# What must not be uploaded as build context.
#
# Everything here is build output that the Dockerfile regenerates inside the
# container. Without this file the context is whatever happens to be lying
# around: running `cargo test` in lib/prolink once leaves a 6.5 GB target/
# directory, and every `docker build` afterwards spends minutes uploading it
# before it can start.
#
# Keep this to derived artefacts only. Excluding a source file here fails the
# build somewhere deep in cmake, with an error that does not mention Docker.

# The Rust workspace's build output. The Dockerfile runs cargo itself, against
# its own cache mount.
lib/prolink/target/

# CMake build trees, wherever someone put theirs. The container configures into
# /build, which is a cache mount and not part of the context at all.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# Editor and tooling leftovers.
.cache/
compile_commands.json
.vscode/
.idea/
